<h2>Our goal</h2><p>We aim to make public information and online banking usable with common assistive technologies and across desktop, tablet and mobile devices.</p>
<h2>Design practices in the overhaul</h2><ul><li>Semantic headings and clearer information hierarchy.</li><li>Keyboard-accessible buttons and navigation where implemented.</li><li>Readable color contrast and restrained use of decorative elements.</li><li>Responsive layouts that avoid forcing desktop-only interaction patterns onto mobile screens.</li><li>Labels and instructions for forms and financial workflows.</li><li>Reduced reliance on color alone to communicate status.</li></ul>
<h2>Known limitations</h2><p>Velmora is undergoing a site-wide overhaul. Some legacy pages and controls may not yet meet the same standard as the new design system, and formal accessibility testing has not yet been completed.</p>
<h2>Need assistance?</h2><p>If a page or banking task is difficult to access, contact <a href="/contact-v2/" style="color:#315978;font-weight:700">Velmora Support</a> and describe the page, device or assistive technology involved so the issue can be investigated.</p>
<h2>Continuous improvement</h2><p>Accessibility should be part of design review, not a one-time page at the end of a redesign. The final site should include testing across keyboard navigation, screen-reader semantics, zoom, responsive behavior and contrast.</p>
